; cluster for all metallic elements and their shared properties.
; what makes a metal a metal: the electron sea.
; valence electrons are delocalised across the whole lattice — not bound
; to individual atoms. this one structural fact explains everything:
; conduction:   electrons flow freely → conducts electricity and heat
; lustre:       free electrons reflect photons → shiny surface
; malleability: layers slide without breaking bonds → can be hammered flat
; ductility:    can be drawn into wires without fracturing
; 
; metallic bond: weaker than covalent, stronger than van der Waals.
; metals form positive ions (cations) — they lose electrons readily.
; most elements in the periodic table are metals (~80%).
; 
; sub-classifications:
; alkali metals    (group 1): Li, Na, K, Rb, Cs — very reactive, soft, low mp
; alkaline earth   (group 2): Be, Mg, Ca, Sr, Ba — harder, higher mp
; transition metals (d-block): Fe, Cu, Zn, Ag, Au, Ti — variable valence, complex ions
; post-transition: Al, Sn, Pb — between transition metals and metalloids
; connections
; 3d / pratibimba

(kosha metals-varga
  (vishesa chemistry-varga)
  (swarupa subanta electron-sea conductor lustrous malleable ductile cation metallic)
  (sthita metallic-bond solid)
  (siddha ionic-bond)
  (yukta heat-transfer alloy oxidation pbr))
